  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256222/assets/8bb00a4e03f3edd35f6e49556fe37e1c468eda2b530716d1c7b35b2dd90ad651.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $2$ units **down** to give $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2.$",
